  ('sestriere-italy', '02F', 'Sestriere', 'Italy', 'Italy''s highest town', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Italian Alps', '{"ski","family","culture","hiking","golf"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Highest municipality in Italy at 2,035 m (Val Susa/Val Chisone pass, Metropolitan City of Turin); ~929 residents, ~20,000 in ski season","Hub of the cross-border Vialattea (Milky Way): 400 km of pistes, 70 lifts, 1,538-2,789 m; 96 km easy / 220 km intermediate / 84 km difficult; links to Montgenevre, France","Built in the 1930s by Giovanni Agnelli (FIAT); the twin cylindrical hotel towers are the village''s founding buildings + symbol; one was part of the 2006 Olympic Village","2006 Turin Winter Olympics: staged all men''s alpine skiing + one of three Olympic Villages; 10 alpine events 12-25 Feb 2006; 287 athletes from 60 nations","Gianni Agnelli World Cup/Olympic slope + floodlit night skiing; ~146 pistes, ~120 with snowmaking; hosted 1997 FIS Alpine World Championships","Still a live World Cup stage: two women''s giant slaloms Feb 2025, both won by Federica Brignone; skiresort.info rates the domain 4.2/5 (outstanding)","Golf Club Sestrieres: 18-hole par-65 course at 2,035 m, one of Europe''s highest; first nine built by Edoardo Agnelli in 1932","2026 = 20th anniversary of Turin 2006; competition runs still used for FIS World Cup events"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (single European emergency, Italy unified — police/ambulance/fire/mountain rescue); legacy 118 medical / 115 fire / 113 police; Soccorso Alpino via 112","hospital":"Ospedale Edoardo Agnelli, Pinerolo (~35 km, ASL TO3, Pronto Soccorso); trauma transfer to Turin, often by helicopter","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (ARPA Piemonte bollettino valanghe, European 5-level AINEVA scale; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide), cold, altitude (base 2,035 m, l