  ('val-gardena-dolomites-italy', '02F', 'Val Gardena', 'Italy', 'The Ladin heart of the Dolomites', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Italian Alps / Dolomites', '{"ski","culture","hiking","family","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Dolomiti Superski: 12 ski areas, 460 lifts, ~1,200 km of piste on one pass; Val Gardena/Alpe di Siusi 84 lifts + 176 km (500+ km connected)","Sella Ronda 44 km circuit (23 km skied, 21 km lift) round the Sella massif linking Val Gardena, Alta Badia, Arabba + Val di Fassa; ~6 hours","Saslong Classic FIS Ski World Cup: downhill since 1972, Super-G since 2002; course 3,446 m / 839 m vertical drop; Camel Humps (130 km/h, 60 m+ jumps, record 88 m 2003)","La Longia longest run in South Tyrol (10 km, 1,273 m vertical, Seceda-Ortisei); season 2025/26 ran 5 Dec 2025-7 Apr 2026; day pass ~EUR 77-86","UNESCO World Heritage Dolomites (inscribed 26 Jun 2009; 9 systems; 142,000 ha); Sassolungo/Sella fossil reefs","Ladin valley: ~85-90% speak Ladin (3rd official language of South Tyrol); woodcarving since 1624; Museum Gherdeina, Ortisei","Three villages: Ortisei 1,236 m, Santa Cristina 1,428 m, Selva 1,563 m; ~10,000 residents","Alpe di Siusi (Seiser Alm) largest high-alpine meadow in Europe (~56 km2, 1,600-2,958 m, 450 km trails); Seceda ridgeline; Sassolungo circuit 17.7 km"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (single European emergency number; South Tyrol calls route to Bolzano control centre; dispatches police/ambulance/fire/mountain rescue)","hospital":"Brixen/Bressanone hospital (Via Dante 51, +39 0472 812111, ~40 km); major trauma Bolzano","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-Dolomite winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (Euregio Avalanche Report avalanche.report/lawinen.report, 5-level European scale; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide), altitude/AMS, cold/whiteout; summer via ferrata (kit + weather); mountain rescu