ookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Abu_Dhabi","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"family","blurb":"the Yas Island marine park and waterpark","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"},{"name":"Liwa / Empty Quarter desert","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the giant dunes of the Rub'' al Khali south of the city","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Abu_Dhabi","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"adventure","blurb":"the giant dunes of the Rub'' al Khali south of the city","when":"year-round","commission":"held - DMC when the gate exists"},{"name":"Desert safari from Abu Dhabi","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"dune drive and Bedouin-camp evening","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Abu_Dhabi","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"dune drive and Bedouin-camp evening","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the current advisory for Abu Dhabi, and can I book it through TravelWell?","a":"The UAE is at U.S. State Department Level 3 - Reconsider Travel, and Abu Dhabi cannot be booked through TravelWell right now. The armed conflict that began 28 February 2026 (U.S./Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; the Strait of Hormuz closed; a State ''depart now'' order on 2 March 2026) is ongoing as of 2026-08-10. TravelWell books Level 3 only through a consent gate that is not built, so no Gulf destination is bookable regardless of level. Re-verify the level and flight picture before any travel.","source":"levels+conflict supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read of the US Embassy UAE alert 4 Jun 2026 + State-advisory press; conflict corroborated 2026-08-10 via F1/FIA cancellation coverage (Sky Sports/PlanetF1 via web search)","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How are flights and airspace affected?","a":"Airports are open but subject to short-notice closures, with renewed UAE airspace restrictions reported 4-11 May 2026. As a concrete example, American Airlines cancelled Philadelphia-Doha through the end of 2026 (restart targeted January 2027). Confirm every segment close to departure.","source":"supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would an Abu Dhabi trip cover once bookable again?","a":"Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, Louvre Abu Dhabi and the Saadiyat museums, Qasr Al Watan, the Corniche, Qasr Al Hosn, Yas Island (Yas Marina Circuit, Ferrari World, Warner Bros World, SeaWorld), and a Liwa/Empty Quarter desert overnight.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Abu_Dhabi (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Abu Dhabi?","a":"October-April is the cool, dry season (and the historic Grand Prix window); summer is very hot, above 40C. Planning-only guidance while the destination is held content-only.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Abu_Dhabi (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"Is the Formula 1 Grand Prix happening?","a":"Treat it as to-be-verified. F1 and the FIA cancelled the 2026 Bahrain and Saudi Arabian Grands Prix (confirmed 15 March 2026) because those Gulf states were struck in the conflict; the Abu Dhabi round''s 2026 status must be confirmed with F1 before routing any traveller.","source":"Sky Sports/PlanetF1 via web search (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Abu Dhabi Travel Advisory & Guide (UAE): Level 3, Safety","meta_description":"Abu Dhabi under a U.S. Level 3 advisory amid the 2026 Gulf conflict - safety, flight disruption, the F1 question, and the sights for when travel resumes. Held content-only.","slug":"abu-dhabi-uae","primary_keyword":"Abu Dhabi travel advisory 2026","long_tail":["Abu Dhabi Level 3","Abu Dhabi Grand Prix 2026","Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque","Louvre Abu Dhabi","UAE airspace disruption"],"search_language":"ar (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["أبوظبي","جامع الشيخ زايد","متحف اللوفر أبوظبي"],"hreflang":["en","ar"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-10"},"booking":{"bin":"content_only_L3_consent_gate_not_built","level":"L3","booking_hold":true,"codes":["L3"],"note":"HELD CONTENT-ONLY. US State Level 3 (Reconsider Travel) for the UAE amid an active regional conflict that began 28 Feb 2026 (US/Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; Hormuz closed; State depart-now for 16 countries 2 Mar 2026), ONGOING as of 2026-08-10. L3 books only via the consent gate, which Sana confirms is NOT built. FAST-MOVING: re-verify State + FCDO before travel. CITATION: level+conflict supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read of the US Embassy UAE alert 4 Jun 2026 + State-advisory press; ae.usembassy.gov returned ''Technical Difficulties'' to a 2026-08-10 re-fetch; conflict corroborated 2026-08-10 via F1/FIA GP-cancellation coverage (Sky Sports/PlanetF1 via web search). EVENT: 2026 Bahrain + Saudi F1 GPs cancelled (F1/FIA 15 Mar 2026); Abu Dhabi GP 2026 status to verify."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-10","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Gulf capital built content-only (safety gap); all SIs future while held; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","name":"entertainment","status":"future"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"family","name":"family","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"HELD - Saadiyat luxury stay + Grand Mosque/Louvre + Liwa desert overnight, via the consent gate once built","why_ultra":"the ultra pull once the advisory de-escalates and the gate exists; not offered while held","earning":"n/a while held","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a while held","mor":"n/a while held","source":"TWW booking doctrine"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-10","hero":{"query":"Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates"},"geo":{"lat":24.45,"lng":54.38}}'::jsonb, 3),
  ('amman-jordan', '04A', 'Amman', 'Jordan', 'The white city on the hills', 'live', 'verified', 'marrakech', 'Jordan & the Levant', '{"culture","deepdive","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["The capital and the country''s gateway - Queen Alia International (AMM), Jordan''s main hub","Roman-era Amman - the hilltop Citadel (Jabal al-Qal''a, Temple of Hercules, Umayyad palace) and a Roman Theatre in the downtown","Jerash nearby - one of the best-preserved Roman provincial cities, ~48 km north, an easy day trip","The start/end of the loop - nearly every Jordan itinerary begins and ends here before Petra, Wadi Rum and the Dead Sea","US Level 3 Reconsider Travel (March 2026); the Level-4 areas are the Syria/Iraq borders - Amman is in the centre-west, far from them","Best season spring and autumn; summer is hot and dry, winters cool with some rain"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (unified - police / ambulance / civil defense); Tourist Police +962 79 550 5755","hospital":"Amman has Jordan''s major hospitals; carry travel-medical + evac insurance","advisory_level":"L3","activity_note":"L3 Reconsider Travel - disclose prominently. Level-4 areas = Syria/Iraq borders (far north/east); Amman is in the centre-west, far from them. Normal big-city care; sun cover at the open Citadel + Jerash.","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to within 3km of the border with Syria."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to Syria."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to Iraq ."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the provinces in Iraq bordering Jordan."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Aqaba Governate FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Aqaba international airport and seaport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Aqaba international airport and seaport."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jordan","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-22T13:47:55+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov (comfortable)","shoulder":"Nov + early Mar","green":"Jun-Aug (hot, dry) + Dec-Feb (cool, some rain)","booking_lead":"city hotels 1-2 mo; peak spring/autumn earlier","off_season_specials":"summer + winter city value; the loop''s gateway year-round","event_peaks":"spring + autumn peak","campaign_start":"sell as the loop''s gateway 2-3 mo out; lead EN + GCC + DE; Roman-heritage + food angles"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Citadel over the white city + the Roman Theatre","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"within the tour","timing":"year-round","draw_rank":1,"timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Temple of Hercules and Umayyad palace on the hill, the theatre cut into the slope below","si":"culture","blurb":"Temple of Hercules and Umayyad palace on the hill, the theatre cut into the slope below","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC 10-15%"},{"name":"A Jerash day trip","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"within the tour","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"colonnaded streets, the oval forum, and arches of one of the Roman world''s best-preserved cities","si":"deepdive","blurb":"colonnaded streets, the oval forum, and arches of one of the Roman world''s best-preserved cities","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"DMC 10-15%"},{"name":"An Amman food walk","si_tag":"culinary","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"within the tour","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"mansaf, knafeh, street food and café culture with a local guide","si":"culinary","blurb":"mansaf, knafeh, street food and café culture with a local guide","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"DMC/affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is there to do in Amman?","a":"Walk the hilltop Citadel over the white city, see the Roman Theatre downtown, eat through a lively food scene, and take a day trip to Jerash - one of the best-preserved Roman provincial cities. It''s the gateway and natural start of the Petra-Wadi Rum-Dead Sea loop.","source":"jordantourplanner.com","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Amman the gateway to Jordan?","a":"Yes - Queen Alia International (AMM) is Jordan''s main hub, about 30 km south of the city, and nearly every itinerary begins and ends in Amman before heading south to Petra, Wadi Rum and the Dead Sea.","source":"jordantourplanner.com","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Amman?","a":"Spring (Mar-May) and autumn (Sep-Nov) are most comfortable. Summer is hot and dry; winters are cool with some rain.","source":"tourism references","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Amman Guide: The Citadel, Jerash & Safety - Gateway to Jordan (2026)","meta_description":"Plan Amman - Jordan''s capital and gateway, the Citadel and Roman Theatre, a Jerash day trip, the food scene, best season spring/autumn, with straight Level-3 safety intel.","slug":"amman-jordan","primary_keyword":"Amman Jordan","long_tail":["Amman Citadel","Roman Theatre Amman","Jerash day trip","is Amman safe","best time to visit Amman","Amman food tour"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Amman","Jabal al-Qal''a","Roman Theatre","Jerash","Queen Alia"],"hreflang":["en","ar","de"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-03"},"booking":{"bin":"book_with_disclosure","level":"L3","codes":["reconsider-travel","regional-tensions","terrorism"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Jordan US Level 3 Reconsider Travel (escalated March 2026, regional US-Iran tensions). Disclose PROMINENTLY; heightened-consent booking. Level-4 Do-Not-Travel areas = Syria + Iraq border strips + Mansheyat al Ghayyath + Ruwayshid - Amman is in the CENTRE-WEST, far from them. Functioning capital + arrival hub. Re-verify each cycle (may revert to L2)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-03","hits":3,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Gateway + culture base: culture (Citadel/Roman Theatre) + deepdive (Jerash/Decapolis) + culinary (Amman food) live; ultra future. sub_region ''Jordan & Petra'' PROPOSED. US L3 - disclose. Gateway node (Queen Alia AMM)."},"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"live","note":"the Citadel (Temple of Hercules, Umayyad palace) + the Roman Theatre; white-stone hills"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"live","note":"Jerash - one of the best-preserved Roman provincial cities, ~48 km north"},{"si":"culinary","name":"culinary","status":"live","note":"mansaf, knafeh, street food + cafe culture; guided food walks"}],"ultra":[{"name":"A luxury Amman base + private Roman-heritage days","why_ultra":"a top city hotel, a private guide across the Citadel, Theatre and Jerash, and a curated food evening before the drive south","earning":"consortia/DMC","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-03","hero":{"query":"Amman, Jordan"},"geo":{"lat":31.9539,"lng":35.9106}}'::jsonb, 4),
  ('aswan-egypt', '04A', 'Aswan', 'Egypt', 'Where the Nile slows', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Egypt & the Nile', '{"river","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Where the Nile slows - feluccas under lateen sails, Philae Temple on its island, the High Dam + Lake Nasser, and Abu Simbel to the south","The southern gate of the Nile cruise - Luxor<->Aswan cruises begin/end here; dahabiyas sail the calm Esna<->Aswan leg","Abu Simbel - Ramses II''s rock temples, 280 km south, by ~3-4 hr dawn road convoy or a ~45-min flight","US L2 Exercise Increased Caution - Aswan + the cruise corridor are in the L2 zone; Do-Not-Travel areas (Sinai interior, Western Desert/Libya border) are far; disclose L2","Sold via Egypt Nile-cruise operators + Aswan DMCs ~10-16%; site tickets non-commissionable pass-through","Best season Oct-Apr (Nov sweet spot), ~25-30C; summer 40C+ - dawn touring"],"safety":{"emergency":"122 police / 123 ambulance / 126 tourist police","hospital":"Aswan hospitals + private clinics; Cairo for major referral; carry travel-medical + evac insurance","advisory_level":"L2","activity_note":"L2 disclose - Aswan + cruise corridor in the L2 zone (Do-Not-Travel areas far away). Main practical risk is summer heat - dawn touring, hydrate. Abu Simbel is a long desert drive - licensed operator, dawn convoy.","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to within 20km of the Egypt-Libya border, except for the town of El Salloum, where we advise against all but essential travel."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the North Sinai Governorate."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to North Sinai Governate due to continuing criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of the South Sinai Governorate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Ismailiyah Governorate east of the Suez Canal."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions, except for: Luxor, Qina, Aswan, Abu Simbel and the Valley of the Kings the Faiyum Governorate the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road the oasis town of Siwa the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis the White Desert and Black Desert the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa) the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the road between Kharga and Baris the road between Baris and Luxor Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and the Bir Tawil Trapezoid."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of South Sinai Governate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel due to criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the parts of the Ismailiyah Governorate which are east of the Suez Canal, due to ongoing military operations against terrorists and criminals."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions due to risks from criminal activity and military operations, except for: Luxor, Qina, Valley of the Kings, Aswan and Abu Simbel the Faiyum Governorate the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road the oasis town of Siwa the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis the White Desert and Black Desert the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa) the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the road between Kharga and Baris the road between Baris and Luxor Tourists who enter the Western Desert areas of Bahariya Oasis, Farafra, the White Desert and Black Desert must apply for permits in advance and use an official guide."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on the road between Al Bawiti and Siwa, including the desert areas near the start of the road in Bahariya."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-08-04T11:10:57+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Oct-Apr (Nov the sweet spot) - comfortable ~25-30C; Christmas/NY high","shoulder":"May + Sep (hotter, softer rates)","green":"Jun-Aug (40C+ - cheapest, quietest)","booking_lead":"cruises + Aswan lodges 3-9 mo for Oct-Apr; dahabiya cabins sell out; shoulder 2-4 mo","off_season_specials":"summer heat value; pair with Luxor + Cairo/GEM","event_peaks":"Oct-Apr; Christmas/NY; N-Hemisphere autumn-winter","campaign_start":"sell Oct-Apr Nile cruises 4-6 mo out; ride the Grand Egyptian Museum (Nov 2025) halo"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Luxor to Aswan Nile cruise (southern gate)","si_tag":"river","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"$350-1,500+/pp; dahabiya ~$1,000-1,500/night","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Luxor↔Aswan cruises begin/end here; dahabiyas sail the calm Esna↔Aswan leg","si":"river","blurb":"Luxor↔Aswan cruises begin/end here; dahabiyas sail the calm Esna↔Aswan leg","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"DMC/cruise 10-16%"},{"name":"Philae Temple + a felucca at golden hour","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"within the tour","timing":"year-round","draw_rank":1,"timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the island Temple of Isis + the Nile''s loveliest sail","si":"culture","blurb":"the island Temple of Isis + the Nile''s loveliest sail","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC 10-15%"},{"name":"Abu Simbel (Ramses II)","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"flight ~$300-400","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"DMC 10-16%"},{"name":"A Nubian village on the Nile","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"low","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":3,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"DMC/community"},{"name":"Old Cataract + Abu Simbel by air","si_tag":"river","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":2,"hook":"the Agatha Christie hotel, a private island temple visit, and Abu Simbel by charter flight. Earning: consortia/DMC. MoR: commissionable","si":"river","blurb":"the Agatha Christie hotel, a private island temple visit, and Abu Simbel by charter flight. Earning: consortia/DMC. MoR: commissionable","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"consortia/DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do I see Abu Simbel from Aswan?","a":"Abu Simbel is 280 km south - reached by a dawn road convoy (~3-4 hrs each way) or a ~45-minute flight. Go early for the light and cooler temperatures, with a licensed operator.","source":"weseektravel.com","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Aswan?","a":"October to April, November the sweet spot - comfortable ~25-30C. Summer tops 40C, so tour at dawn and hydrate.","source":"egypttoursportal.com","si_tag":"river"},{"q":"Cruise or stay in Aswan?","a":"Both - Aswan is the southern end of the Luxor-Aswan cruise. Add a night for Philae Temple, a felucca sail at sunset, and a Nubian village visit.","source":"responsiblevacation.com","si_tag":"river"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Aswan Guide: Philae, Abu Simbel & the Nile - Best Time & Safety","meta_description":"Plan Aswan - Philae Temple, the High Dam, Abu Simbel, Nubian villages and a felucca on the Nile, the southern gate of the Luxor-Aswan cruise, best season Oct-Apr, with real safety and timing intel.","slug":"aswan-egypt","primary_keyword":"Aswan Egypt","long_tail":["Abu Simbel from Aswan","Philae Temple","Aswan felucca Nile","Luxor to Aswan cruise","best time to visit Aswan","is Aswan safe"],"search_language":"ar","local_keywords":["Aswan","Philae","Abu Simbel","Nile","Nubia"],"hreflang":["en","ar"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-03"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":["exercise-increased-caution","terrorism","crime"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Egypt US L2 Exercise Increased Caution - the Nile corridor (Aswan, the cruise, Abu Simbel) is in the L2 zone. Do-Not-Travel carve-out excludes N/Middle Sinai (except Sharm el-Sheikh by air) + the Western Desert/Libya border area (L4), far from Aswan. Disclose L2. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-03","hits":3,"mi